u=\\text{arcsec}(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of $u$ as the variable, we have $\\sqrt{5}x.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=\\sqrt{5}x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\sqrt{5}\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{5{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{|\\sqrt{5}x|\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{5}x)^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}u}{|u|\\sqrt{{u}^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec }u+C \\\\  & =\\text{arcsec}(\\sqrt{5}x)+C\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058396/state.json" "file_sha256" "007cc25a06b3c4fa173bf522da1bef1b3fe012a2be9b719466b8d5cbd343bba9"} {"question" "q-114051" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058396/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0f93b9a3f902ac849992de95124c7f0a813db318b9252d08098d838c9ff9b71e"} {"question" "q-114051" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058396/state.json" "file_sha256" "007cc25a06b3c4fa173bf522da1bef1b3fe012a2be9b719466b8d5cbd343bba9"} {"question" "q-114051" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "5\\,\\text{arcsec}(5x)+C"] ["math" "5\\,\\text{arcsec}(\\sqrt{5}x)+C"] ["math" "\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{arcsec}(\\sqrt{5}x)+C"] ["math" "\\text{arcsec}(5x)+C"] ["math" "\\text{arcsec}(\\sqrt{5}x)+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058396/state.json" "file_sha256" "007cc25a06b3c4fa173bf522da1bef1b3fe012a2be9b719466b8d5cbd343bba9"} {"question" "q-114051" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\text{arcsec}(\\sqrt{5}x)+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058396/state.json" "file_sha256" "007cc25a06b3c4fa173bf522da1bef1b3fe012a2be9b719466b8d5cbd343bba9"} {"question" "q-351834" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-0.2}^{0.2}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3-75{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058396/state.json" "file_sha256" "007cc25a06b3c4fa173bf522da1bef1b3fe012a2be9b719466b8d5cbd343bba9"} {"question" "q-351834" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-0.2}^{0.2}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3-75{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{-0.2}^{0.2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3\\cdot (1-25{x}^{2})}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3}}{\\int }_{-0.2}^{0.2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-25{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{-0.2}^{0.2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(5x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(u)+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(5x)}^{2}.$   \n\nSo, let's substitute $u=5x.$ Differentiating, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=5\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $-0.2$ | $0.2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $-1$ | $1$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-0.2}^{0.2}\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3-75{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{-0.2}^{0.2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(5x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot (\\frac{1}{5}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{5}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{5}\\,\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{5}(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(1)-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{5}(\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\,\\pi }{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058396/state.json" "file_sha256" "007cc25a06b3c4fa173bf522da1bef1b3fe012a2be9b719466b8d5cbd343bba9"} {"question" "q-351834" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058396/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0f93b9a3f902ac849992de95124c7f0a813db318b9252d08098d838c9ff9b71e"} {"question" "q-351834" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058396/state.json" "file_sha256" "007cc25a06b3c4fa173bf522da1bef1b3fe012a2be9b719466b8d5cbd343bba9"} {"question" "q-351834" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\pi}{5}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058396/state.json" "file_sha256" "007cc25a06b3c4fa173bf522da1bef1b3fe012a2be9b719466b8d5cbd343bba9"} {"question" "q-351839" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{12}{3+27{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\operatorname{arctan}⁡($\n{{field-2}}$)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058396/state.json" "file_sha256" "007cc25a06b3c4fa173bf522da1bef1b3fe012a2be9b719466b8d5cbd343bba9"} {"question" "q-351839" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that we can rewrite this integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{12}{3+27{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=4{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{1}{1+9{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse tangent,\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have $9{x}^{2}=(3x)^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=3x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $12$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{12}{3+27{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =4{\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{1}{1+(3x)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{\\int }_{0}^{12}\\frac{1}{1+{u}^{2}}\\,\\cdot (\\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{12}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{1+{u}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡u{|}_{0}^{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(12)-\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\,arctan\\,(12)\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058396/state.json" "file_sha256" "007cc25a06b3c4fa173bf522da1bef1b3fe012a2be9b719466b8d5cbd343bba9"} {"question" "q-351839" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058396/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0f93b9a3f902ac849992de95124c7f0a813db318b9252d08098d838c9ff9b71e"} {"question" "q-351839" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058396/state.json" "file_sha256" "007cc25a06b3c4fa173bf522da1bef1b3fe012a2be9b719466b8d5cbd343bba9"} {"question" "q-351839" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{4}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058396/state.json" "file_sha256" "007cc25a06b3c4fa173bf522da1bef1b3fe012a2be9b719466b8d5cbd343bba9"} {"question" "q-351839" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058396/state.json" "file_sha256" "007cc25a06b3c4fa173bf522da1bef1b3fe012a2be9b719466b8d5cbd343bba9"} {"question" "q-351839" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "12"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14058396/state.json" "file_sha256" "007cc25a06b3c4fa173bf522da1bef1b3fe012a2be9b719466b8d5cbd343bba9"}] "usage" {"q-2507" [] "q-114051" [] "q-49548" []} "basis" 1896 "retractions" [[17592186064792 :question